# #279: an art pass after which nothing changed owes no other. The
# owner's 0.8.0 and 0.8.1 logs: after "art pass done", "art again owed
# ... rg=1" started another full pass about every 100 s for as long as
# the unit sat idle, each pass building the same panels again on the
# CPU (16 of 32 there, twice a pass). Cause: a panel whose source differs
# from its album's thumbnail record (a synced track with embedded art,
# #225 Q1; or a record from before the two-ended signature) never
# matched it, so it was built again each pass into a new slot, the set
# was no longer grouped, and the regroup owed the next pass.
# Here: a synced library with such albums ("0 Both"), its art made, then
# the unit stopped and idle past the boot's 3 minutes (the regroup window
# open) and four quiet minutes more: no further pass, no panel built
# again. Red on 09791e053f: "art again owed ... rg=1", a pass that builds
# the same 6 panels twice.
#   IPODCTL_SCRIPT=ipodctl-idle-nopass.script tests/perf/ipodctl_sim.sh 300
# golden: skip
# timeout: 1200
# logbetween: a0 q1 no art build start
# logbetween: a0 q1 no art again owed
# logbetween: a0 q1 no art build panel key=
# logbetween: q0 q1 no art panel regroup
wait 4000
wait_db 3000000
art_wait 3000000
ab_mark a0          # the first pass done: nothing changes from here
backlight_expire    # idle and stopped
wait 200000         # past 3 minutes of uptime: the window opens
art_wait 600000     # what the window owes (a regroup, a pool top-up)
ab_mark w0
art_wait 600000     # (a pass it owed in turn: none after the fix)
ab_mark q0
wait 240000         # four minutes idle: nothing more to do
ab_mark q1
key MENU
wait 1500
shot end
quit
